    "id": "rate_half_kb_m2_r4_coordinate_positive_ramified_loop_multiplicity_exclusion",
    "title": "KoalaBear m2 r4 positive ramified-loop multiplicity exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "local complete-source order 2 versus order 4 and the ordinary Vieta sum row force a global positive loop cap of one",
    "statement": "At a ramified positive antipodal star where B_1 is nonzero, exactly the two antipodal target rows vanish and each has local order one, whereas the complete-source square requires order four at the doubled branch fiber. Hence every ramified loop is the B_1 zero; the ordinary Vieta sum row gives the same condition at every nonramified loop. Since B_1 is nonzero linear, a positive packet has at most one loop over all twelve complete fibers. Every two-/three-common-loop row is empty, a one-common-loop row has no outside loop, and a zero-common-loop row has at most one outside loop.",
